From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 10:28:07 +0200
Subject: clocksource/drivers/sun4i: Never program a zero interval

The driver registers min_delta_ticks = TIMER_SYNC_TICKS and subtracts
TIMER_SYNC_TICKS from evt in set_next_event, so a minimum-delta
program from the clockevents core writes a zero interval.  The
hardware never fires on a zero interval: the counter is left parked
at zero, or sometimes frozen with a stale non-zero count - the state
that defeated the original check_armed() and stopped the tick for
good.  This showed up as a storm of evt=3/intval=0 arm failures under
heavy interrupt load (expired hrtimers make the core fall back to
min_delta_ticks), and matches the intval=0 read back from a wedged
machine over /dev/mem.

Floor the programmed interval at one tick and raise the registered
minimum so the core does not request an interval the timer cannot
generate.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/clocksource/timer-sun4i.c | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clocksource/timer-sun4i.c b/drivers/clocksource/timer-sun4i.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/clocksource/timer-sun4i.c
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/timer-sun4i.c
@@ -205,10 +205,14 @@ static int sun4i_clkevt_next_event(unsigned long evt,
 				   struct clock_event_device *clkevt)
 {
 	struct timer_of *to = to_timer_of(clkevt);
+	unsigned long delay;
 	int ret;
 
+	/* The timer never fires with a zero interval. */
+	delay = evt > TIMER_SYNC_TICKS + 1 ? evt - TIMER_SYNC_TICKS : 1;
+
 	sun4i_clkevt_time_stop(timer_of_base(to), 0);
-	sun4i_clkevt_time_setup(timer_of_base(to), 0, evt - TIMER_SYNC_TICKS);
+	sun4i_clkevt_time_setup(timer_of_base(to), 0, delay);
 	sun4i_clkevt_time_start(timer_of_base(to), 0, false);
 
 	ret = sun4i_clkevt_check_armed(timer_of_base(to), 0);
@@ -341,7 +345,7 @@ static int __init sun4i_timer_init(struct device_node *node)
 	sun4i_timer_clear_interrupt(timer_of_base(&to));
 
 	clockevents_config_and_register(&to.clkevt, timer_of_rate(&to),
-					TIMER_SYNC_TICKS, 0xffffffff);
+					TIMER_SYNC_TICKS + 1, 0xffffffff);
 
 	/* Enable timer0 interrupt */
 	val = readl(timer_of_base(&to) + TIMER_IRQ_EN_REG);
-- 
Armbian

